{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26969 - PROTEIN:5026",
  "verbalization": "Isoriccardin C appears to have a complex relationship with COLO-800, as it is linked through multiple pathways to Caspase-2, which in turn targets various molecules that ultimately have a target of COLO-800. The first pathway connects Isoriccardin C to Caspase-2, which is then targeted by N-Acetyl-Serine and 3,6-Anhydro-2-deoxy-beta-d-arabino-hexofuranose, both of which direct to COLO-800. The second pathway links Isoriccardin C to Caspase-2, which is targeted by budesonide, which also directs to COLO-800. These pathways suggest that Isoriccardin C may influence COLO-800 through a series of molecular interactions involving caspase-2 and other targets. The evidence supports a potential mechanism where Isoriccardin C modulates Caspase-2 activity, which in turn affects the downstream targets that ultimately interact with COLO-800. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Isoriccardin C in modulating cellular processes that lead to the interaction with COLO-800.",
